cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these scripts or data, please cite the paper below and Honghu.jl."
title: "Scripts and data for \"An Adaptive Reduced Speed of Light Approximation\""
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Chong-Chong
    family-names: He
    email: chongchong.he@anu.edu.au
    affiliation: Australian National University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2332-8178"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/chongchonghe/paper-ARSA"
abstract: >-
  The scripts and data that make every figure, table and quoted number of
  He, Krumholz and Wibking, "An Adaptive Reduced Speed of Light Approximation":
  the linear analysis of the reduced speed of light approximation (RSLA) and
  of the adaptive RSLA (ARSA), the numerical tests run with Honghu.jl v0.1.0,
  and the estimates of Table 1. One command, ./run_all.sh, rebuilds them.
keywords:
  - radiation hydrodynamics
  - reduced speed of light approximation
  - M1 closure
  - reproducibility
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Honghu.jl: three-dimensional radiation hydrodynamics in Julia"
    authors:
      - given-names: Chong-Chong
        family-names: He
    version: 0.1.0
